<title>BOSNIA: BOSNIA MAY RETAIL PRICES UP 2.9 PCT M/M, 13.7 Y/Y.</title>
<headline>BOSNIA MAY RETAIL PRICES UP 2.9 PCT M/M, 13.7 Y/Y.</headline>
<dateline>SARAJEVO 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Statistics Bureau of Bosnia's Moslem-Croat federation issued the following economic indicator details on Monday.</p>
<p>    BOSNIA RETAIL PRICES		 MAY    APRIL   MAY 96</p>
<p>    Monthly change (pct)		 +2.9    +2.9     +1.7</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change		 +13.7   +11.9    -25.2</p>
<p>NOTES -- The data cover 51 percent of Bosnia-Hercegovina territory. Data for remaining 49 percent are not available. Retail prices in Jan-May 1997 rose 11.7 percent compared to the same period in 1996, the office said. -- Sarajevo newsroom, +387-71-663-864.</p>
</text>
